More on this in a bit, but first:


What alignment do you favor?  It seems to me that the best alignment to be
is Lawful, for the following reasons:
1) Two of the best artifacts (Mjollnir, Excaliber) available from god. 
2) Can convert any altar to Lawful, which is good because:
3) Lawful altars make holy water, i.e., blessings.

Any dissention on this point?  Chaotic characters *do* have a good chance of
getting Stormbringer from their god.  But unholy water is so... useless.

Given that Lawful is the best alignment to have, I always try to convert to 
Lawfulness as soon as I have a lawful altar and enough monsters in range to
sacrifice to get over the lawful god's initial displeasure.

Which leads to the following minor spoiler:



What if you are Neutral or Chaotic and your game has not produced any Lawful
altars?  The trick is to find a helm of opposite alignment, and put it on,
changing your alignment to Lawful.  (Neutral characters may have to take it 
off and put it back on many times to get Lawful.)  Then you can convert any
altar that you find, and start making holy water.  You can also take off the 
helm (reverting to your old alignment) and find a unicorn to sacrifice to
permanently change to Lawfulness.

Unicorn horns are extremely useful to turn hallucination, sickness, and 
blindness potions into water, which can then be blessed on the altar.  
Similarly, a wand of cancellation will turn as many junky potions as you have 
(of any type) into water to be blessed.


